{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Now you shall see, etc.</b> You pondered My ways — not like Abraham, to whom I said ״כִּי בְיִצְחָק יִקָּרֵא לְךָ זָרַע״ (Genesis 21), and afterward I said to him ״הַעֲלֵהוּ לְעוֹלָה״ and he did not ponder after Me; therefore <b>now you shall see.</b> What is done to Pharaoh you shall see — but not what is done to the seven nations' kings when I bring them into the land (Sanhedrin 111)." "<b>For with a strong hand he will send them out.</b> Because of My strong hand that will prevail upon him, he will send them out." "<b>And with a strong hand he will drive them from his land.</b> Against their will — Israel's — he will drive them out; they will not have time to prepare provisions for themselves. And so it says ״וַתֶּחֱזַק מִצְרַיִם עַל הָעָם וגוֹ״ (Exodus 12)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:50:53.444893323Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}